\title{STARKs: Plonky3, Stwo, and Circle STARKs}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    [AIR](dhsorens-002U) plus [FRI](dhsorens-0037), over a small field, as a reusable toolkit rather
    than a single protocol. This is the layer the [Rust-to-Lean extraction work](dhsorens-0043)
    targets: [Plonky3](dhsorens-plonky3) in Lean, with proofs about what it computes.
}

\p{
    Questions this page should answer:
    \ul{
        \li{The STARK protocol end to end: trace, constraints, quotient, commitment, low-degree
        test.}
        \li{[Plonky3](dhsorens-plonky3) as a toolkit — what is configurable (field, hash, PCS,
        folding factor) and what is fixed.}
        \li{Stwo and the circle domain: Mersenne31 has no large smooth subgroup, so what replaces it
        and what changes in the constraint system.}
        \li{Circle STARKs' vanishing polynomials and the extra care their boundary constraints
        need.}
        \li{Where the two toolkits agree, since both consume an AIR — and what that means for
        [Clean](dhsorens-002Y) targeting both.}
    }
}

\p{
    Sources: [Plonky3](https://github.com/Plonky3/Plonky3),
    [stwo](https://github.com/starkware-libs/stwo), Buterin,
    [Exploring circle STARKs](https://vitalik.eth.limo/general/2024/07/23/circlestarks.html).
}
